## Context
Audit: `conception/2026-10-29-memory-system-audit.md` (PR #1984) R8. Brood, the exit from memory to procedure, has never run on the harness itself.
Crystallisation needs an explicit author request with a destination (AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary).

## Scope
Run brood once after the rebuilt hoard (1349), scoped to lesson candidates in decaying topics.
List the candidates for the author; implement nothing without the request.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One brood run report, listing candidates with sources, or "no change" with reasons

## Rule-candidate lane (author, 2026-10-29)
The native-note probe (1349 § Input design) found that 41% of the harness's native Claude notes,
and 64% of a sample from AEDIST's, prescribe behaviour that `rules/` does not hold: the author's
working rules live in native memory. Smelt files them under Commission as rulings and never
promotes them. This brood run lists them as rule candidates: the ruling, its source note and
date, the rule file it would join, and any conflict with a current rule (three known, for
example `prose_edits_on_main` versus `rules/git.md`). The author decides each one; promotion
needs the explicit request with a destination (AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary).
Extra exit criterion:
- [ ] Rule candidates from the drained native notes listed with source, destination and conflicts

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise: blocker 1349 closed 2026-10-31. Brood is author-invoked (`disable-model-invocation`); the author's /raid over this ticket is the explicit request, scoped by the ticket: a report only, no implementation.
- Output: one brood report with lesson candidates and the rule-candidate lane (ruling, source note and date, destination rule file, conflicts), filed under conception/ or memory/evidence/.

